D7 - SUBTITLE / DIALOGUE-LINE SYSTEM (DRAFT PATCH, NOT BUILT, NOT VERIFIED)
Veil of Succession - queue item Q7 of AUTOMATION_AGENDA.md

This file is a unified diff against main. Everything above the first
"diff --git" line is a comment and is ignored by git apply.

  APPLY:   git apply Patches/subtitles.diff
  UNDO:    git apply -R Patches/subtitles.diff

Companion: Patches/subtitles_TESTPLAN.md - what to build, what to look at,
and every open question. NOTHING HERE HAS BEEN COMPILED OR SEEN RUNNING.
This was written headlessly with no engine, so treat it as a proposal.

WHAT IT DOES
  UMissionSubsystem gains a one-channel dialogue system: a cue library, a
  priority/interrupt model, repeat rules (once / re-arm / bank), multi-line
  chains, and an active-line clock driven by FTickableGameObject.
  AVeilHUD renders the active line as a wrapped, faded, speaker-coloured
  subtitle block at the bottom centre of the screen.

FILES
  NEW  Source/VeilOfSuccession/VeilDialogue.h    cue types + tuning constants
  NEW  Source/VeilOfSuccession/VeilDialogue.cpp  the 84-line built-in registry
  NEW  Content/Data/VeilDialogueCues.csv         same 84 lines, importable as
                                                 a UDataTable (row struct:
                                                 FVeilDialogueCue)
  MOD  Source/VeilOfSuccession/MissionSubsystem.h/.cpp   the channel
  MOD  Source/VeilOfSuccession/VeilHUD.h/.cpp            the rendering

CANON
  All 84 lines are the canon text of Docs/MISSION_SCRIPTS.md as organised in
  Docs/drafts/darya_earpiece.md. They were script-checked verbatim against
  those two files (0 mismatches) after folding typographic punctuation to
  ASCII, which the rest of this codebase uses. No canon file was modified.

